#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188123 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b14ef98-8122-512a-9cce-6e44392959d8" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "b0e16600-3365-562f-8cc8-bf25e0c1638a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3144" :question/problem "Express $\\tan^2 x\\sec^2 x - \\tan^4 x +1$ in terms of $\\sec x$ only." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x+1 & ={tan}^{2}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)+1 \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot (1)+1 \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can use $(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡x+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x\\sec^2 x - \\tan^4 x +1 = \\sec^2 x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188124 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eda44360-52ec-59f7-98b4-f8d866a465e9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Alternate Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "91980d9e-0e4f-546e-b9ee-3117c4950aed" :question/math-academy-id "e-3455" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan^2 \\theta}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}\\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan^2 \\theta} =  \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue} 1} = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan^2 \\theta} = 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188125 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring Alternative Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "915ff3d9-c631-5134-82ff-58dbf0167602" :question/math-academy-id "e-3463" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}1}{\\sec{\\theta}+\\tan{\\theta}} = \\dfrac{\\color{blue}\\sec^2{\\theta} - \\tan^2{\\theta}}{\\sec{\\theta} + \\tan{\\theta}}\n$$\n\nNext, we can further simplify our expression by factoring the numerator as a difference of squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )}}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta} =  \\sec{\\theta} - \\tan{\\theta}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eda44360-52ec-59f7-98b4-f8d866a465e9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Alternate Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3797355d-64b4-5573-99d6-706d341e9f93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285259} {:answer/id #uuid "74929d30-c5fc-5fd0-acaf-730629c4e6a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285260} {:answer/id #uuid "cebeb8f2-7425-5baf-9240-281aa78ca5ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285261} {:answer/id #uuid "5438d4df-7d9e-5f8e-a4ad-8afb86bfc403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285262} {:answer/id #uuid "f85a09b5-30ce-58bb-8e56-4465b14bd515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74929d30-c5fc-5fd0-acaf-730629c4e6a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285260} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceea422c-f036-5d50-925c-7f2352d16112" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ccbc348b-5678-5234-b4b7-a8ceafb9b1d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-120652" :question/problem "$\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-1+{sin}^{2}⁡x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-1+{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-1+{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n1-{sin}^{2}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nUsing the above identity, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-1+{sin}^{2}⁡x & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-(1-{sin}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡x}}{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡x}}-\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-2{cos}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-1+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1-2{cos}^{2}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285264 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eda44360-52ec-59f7-98b4-f8d866a465e9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Alternate Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d689bc08-861c-5471-a056-d3833566386a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285266} {:answer/id #uuid "fa87b35d-8097-59ce-923d-eeb51e395f5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285267} {:answer/id #uuid "06ed0be9-0072-54fa-a9c8-4c930a1faaf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285268} {:answer/id #uuid "24d509a1-1d10-5cf6-8196-4ad0952d894a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285269} {:answer/id #uuid "b7177ee3-b0a6-5476-9df6-cfaea25aa6a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d689bc08-861c-5471-a056-d3833566386a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285266} :answer-field/id #uuid "f10c1005-47fc-5b9e-8be9-eb1b3019f5fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f06ce1a-3e13-5308-9a14-0ac2fdb59c56" :question/math-academy-id "q-120655" :question/problem "$\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}=\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nUsing the above identity, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring Alternative Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "620c5466-603d-566a-955a-98e168b705da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285273} {:answer/id #uuid "007808dc-08a1-5b55-a3c3-c37fcb6e4989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285274} {:answer/id #uuid "a960312e-d793-5da9-a49d-a65deb66f22d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285275} {:answer/id #uuid "b1f0429e-e2a0-5beb-9fa9-deb2343a3d0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285276} {:answer/id #uuid "de81087b-986c-5246-bfbc-3a5c6694b741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1f0429e-e2a0-5beb-9fa9-deb2343a3d0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285276} :answer-field/id #uuid "01714cfe-c53b-536e-93ff-e281bf202852" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3a5bb470-9e62-50a9-851a-d9d6f1fb0a5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-120660" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1=\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression by factoring the numerator as a difference of squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1 & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}}-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring Alternative Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "197e5d2b-0490-5d1e-9df6-fe2ed00b2317" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285280} {:answer/id #uuid "5727e43e-f671-5d86-b524-8654d84c8155" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285281} {:answer/id #uuid "f7544206-a06f-5bda-91c9-419443e0139f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285282} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb6ed41-ea55-5677-bdf6-5a12562d5af4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285283} {:answer/id #uuid "b348568c-3151-59f2-b11c-51c1e0c89d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "197e5d2b-0490-5d1e-9df6-fe2ed00b2317" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285280} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc64d67f-d02d-5bca-b92c-916a37642079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4124205-8bba-50c1-a590-cbcdb14b2bc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-120661" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}=\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}\n$$\n\nNext, we can further simplify our expression by factoring it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)^{2}} & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)}{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b14ef98-8122-512a-9cce-6e44392959d8" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa75f0f7-9024-57fb-b774-3daae61d1657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285287} {:answer/id #uuid "00523e45-1eb6-594c-b159-e3ed07485eaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285288} {:answer/id #uuid "8b346724-4fc0-5285-880c-cd0e1c774f4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285289} {:answer/id #uuid "143756e1-2d1c-5415-8d60-ce7e51a468e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285290} {:answer/id #uuid "c278de93-309a-580c-bf6e-c58771d04fae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c278de93-309a-580c-bf6e-c58771d04fae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285291} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6175e4b-9b4b-5387-8288-ff45b0975c81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4d22fb34-9950-5741-aa15-32ef6c45e5c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-120666" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +1}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +1}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression and use again $(2)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ({tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }({tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)}{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & =({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)-1 \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +1}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b14ef98-8122-512a-9cce-6e44392959d8" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac8a12e0-b2ce-5467-b8ef-e089b52f02b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cot}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285294} {:answer/id #uuid "fc2976f6-7e0e-53cf-a636-74b5b3746675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285295} {:answer/id #uuid "c91aef0e-9e07-5889-b264-09e4c1ce89e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285296} {:answer/id #uuid "1bbfc53f-c97f-5831-a9fb-e8b16871725d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285297} {:answer/id #uuid "d528e988-94d4-503a-8a85-0778dfd22712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cot}^{2}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac8a12e0-b2ce-5467-b8ef-e089b52f02b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cot}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285294} :answer-field/id #uuid "e65a0305-9619-57b3-b126-4a8a86027b26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "92a99f57-2296-5ef9-bfb2-645e5be59829" :question/math-academy-id "q-120667" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{4}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{4}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1} & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{4}⁡x-({tan}^{2}⁡x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{4}⁡x-{sec}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{4}⁡x-{sec}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡x}}{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡x}({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x})}^{2} \\\\  & ={cot}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{4}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1}={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b14ef98-8122-512a-9cce-6e44392959d8" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "959fcaa3-2a20-5911-bc01-e05dc9a6e611" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285301} {:answer/id #uuid "9c274948-0224-5037-a192-3ba9ae989063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285302} {:answer/id #uuid "bd2b36bd-4c37-5b73-b996-1a0684637e40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285303} {:answer/id #uuid "b21741da-13f0-5f26-8c92-b40d6cb5d2f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285304} {:answer/id #uuid "cc04feb7-3169-5f7e-8b7c-361f57dc70f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc04feb7-3169-5f7e-8b7c-361f57dc70f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285305} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7b7afa4-108f-5add-83b2-6198e829da9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ca727bea-1546-5336-bc45-6177d622e77c" :question/math-academy-id "q-120807" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x+1}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x+1} & =\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can use $(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x+1} & =\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x})}^{2} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x+1}={cos}^{2}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eda44360-52ec-59f7-98b4-f8d866a465e9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Alternate Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3075ce6-8434-5703-94f1-5441118c69b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285308} {:answer/id #uuid "aeddb186-dfb6-5962-9a30-24150d28222e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285309} {:answer/id #uuid "138fc64c-0334-5db0-8490-440786fd612e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285310} {:answer/id #uuid "3eec5e1f-bace-5c73-adb9-6e6b9f706175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285311} {:answer/id #uuid "31fc83d4-e9fc-5c19-91f4-a8dca18637d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3075ce6-8434-5703-94f1-5441118c69b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285308} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4c4c9e5-b961-5cf5-8f91-02b6c03f7fe9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a45a07ce-ef6d-5305-907c-a2cbfdebbfff" :question/math-academy-id "q-23597" :question/problem "Simplify $(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1)={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\nThen, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1)={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eda44360-52ec-59f7-98b4-f8d866a465e9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Alternate Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b24dde4d-da9c-562d-9c7e-5cc08bd679aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285315} {:answer/id #uuid "81ab952d-d927-5dcf-ad5f-2766a010eef1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285316} {:answer/id #uuid "ca4b5d87-d89c-5b1e-85d9-ed37a537e25a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285317} {:answer/id #uuid "97b5a8e8-e030-5e3a-97cd-a0e7061be567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285318} {:answer/id #uuid "130b0653-8d24-5c9d-9612-1d2c45de5c97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca4b5d87-d89c-5b1e-85d9-ed37a537e25a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285317} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8d778ec-9a4f-52fd-bb35-a664a5bd3d16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "865215e5-5e9a-5d33-9549-0e100dbb1d6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-23796" :question/problem "${csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ({tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following identities: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the parentheses and use the above identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ({tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{1}{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }}\\cdot \\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }-1 \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ({tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring Alternative Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "608ffb16-f713-5b8c-9a14-64b55486cfe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285322} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf669aa-aaa8-5dc3-9ed1-7b4bf8fb23e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285323} {:answer/id #uuid "502e8efa-9499-5b4d-8535-b5555f676f9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285324} {:answer/id #uuid "a86b481d-c878-577e-ab56-361bec208dd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285325} {:answer/id #uuid "1836c3e5-8364-549e-9400-dcc12cfe17bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "502e8efa-9499-5b4d-8535-b5555f676f9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285324} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c5b65c5-879b-54d2-9ec3-be2a8df72f1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "67303de5-29d5-5458-8cb0-e20946888cb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-23853" :question/problem "Simplify ${sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{4}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we can simplify our expression by factoring it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{4}⁡x & =({sec}^{2}⁡x)^{2}-2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x+({tan}^{2}⁡x)^{2} \\\\  & ={({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}^{2} & ={(1)}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{4}⁡x=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring Alternative Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2802e5f4-5b46-55c7-a7bd-92e09fd9230c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285329} {:answer/id #uuid "48d825fe-bae5-5439-86d0-4b62293907aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285330} {:answer/id #uuid "858395bd-093a-58cf-8275-46cbf6e00545" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285331} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b4c8d3-ea49-5f91-9764-b50259112ddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285332} {:answer/id #uuid "83491247-e8cf-5ee6-bbb9-32bb5328c33a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2802e5f4-5b46-55c7-a7bd-92e09fd9230c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285329} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f3cbdd3-f6f2-5473-bf5f-477632f7eb86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a822db5b-3650-546e-a7db-6d56a65098a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-43292" :question/problem "${csc}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following identities: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nUsing the above identity, we can simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\frac{{sin}^{4}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }}\\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1) & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={tan}^{4}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ={tan}^{4}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring Alternative Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc77baf0-4469-503f-83a6-d2de86933824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x - \\tan x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187815} {:answer/id #uuid "e700d2fc-70b5-5a70-b0dd-3b3ea2254d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x + \\tan x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187816} {:answer/id #uuid "eaaddfa3-7d18-5664-bd11-d1c5e78c8bdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (\\sec x + \\tan x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187817} {:answer/id #uuid "eb07bb9a-bb2c-5948-870c-7b151292816a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (\\sec x - \\tan x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187818} {:answer/id #uuid "234f9771-28c3-5e21-b971-7d49f78c6485" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e700d2fc-70b5-5a70-b0dd-3b3ea2254d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x + \\tan x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187816} :answer-field/id #uuid "39849032-fe5b-5aac-888e-42054128fb15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187814}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "98997ad6-1ba3-510a-969b-b1a491e9f8b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-65392" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}=\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the numerator as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285334 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b14ef98-8122-512a-9cce-6e44392959d8" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9b3860c-017c-5c8e-a388-640d97df4141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{4}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285336} {:answer/id #uuid "62689ad4-2ff9-53ab-9768-9181d448ba83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285337} {:answer/id #uuid "3b2013b6-9ef4-59d9-84e3-982959024707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x{tan}^{4}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285338} {:answer/id #uuid "69fd8dd9-ef8e-5502-9940-5b0376247156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285339} {:answer/id #uuid "3d57c2cb-5c36-51e2-b732-f51854942bf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62689ad4-2ff9-53ab-9768-9181d448ba83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285337} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2a1b999-0ee9-52a8-807d-3b9e35626acd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be326033-9a6d-52c4-b689-ab656ecffefe" :question/math-academy-id "q-65401" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1+{tan}^{2}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1+{sec}^{2}⁡x-1\n$$\n\nNext, we can further simplify our expression and use again $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1+{sec}^{2}⁡x-1 & ={sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+\\cancel{1}+{sec}^{2}⁡x-\\cancel{1} \\\\  & ={sec}^{4}⁡x-{sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot ({sec}^{2}⁡x-1) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eda44360-52ec-59f7-98b4-f8d866a465e9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Alternate Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cc9083d-e297-576b-9e1e-0eb4eb479bbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285343} {:answer/id #uuid "27274b88-5b8d-5d10-833c-536c65e2ea3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285344} {:answer/id #uuid "793dd14a-2fd2-5512-b9a8-1034f4e55a20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285345} {:answer/id #uuid "9243f118-5dbf-5669-a3fa-6fcbcb421146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285346} {:answer/id #uuid "5045282d-d179-523e-9b3b-85988254690f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9243f118-5dbf-5669-a3fa-6fcbcb421146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285346} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fff5922-d168-5a6c-983f-c1ce7121dff4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84160774-04b0-5e68-a9e4-2c2792c403e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-65402" :question/problem "Simplify $(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nThen, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b14ef98-8122-512a-9cce-6e44392959d8" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b8bb6df-9d0a-5566-b621-60c49d2b8ca0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{4}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285350} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3dee10-5f8c-544b-9e6a-53608c51bcc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+{tan}^{4}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285351} {:answer/id #uuid "862023a2-8a4b-56e8-a6df-4cfbcec868d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{4}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285352} {:answer/id #uuid "34e45809-77ac-55fe-a9de-2b7b36595853" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285353} {:answer/id #uuid "0439e24f-a093-5095-996e-597a02208d68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "862023a2-8a4b-56e8-a6df-4cfbcec868d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{4}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285352} :answer-field/id #uuid "16787a52-f969-5089-817e-b7e93ce3f1b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c231bcb-00f5-5c10-87ba-efe156f326e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-74167" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1 & ={tan}^{2}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)-1 \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡x({tan}^{2}⁡x)-1 \\\\  & ={tan}^{4}⁡x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{4}⁡x-1.\n$$"}]}
